# FacePrep Backend

Express + SQLite backend for the FacePrep exam platform.

---

## Folder structure

```
faceprep-backend/
├── src/
│   ├── server.js              ← Entry point — Express app + middleware
│   ├── db.js                  ← SQLite schema (7 tables, indexes, WAL)
│   ├── seed.js                ← Seed DB with assessments, questions, users
│   ├── middleware/
│   │   └── auth.js            ← JWT sign/verify, requireAuth, requireAdmin
│   └── routes/
│       ├── auth.js            ← POST /login /register /logout, GET /me
│       ├── assessments.js     ← GET /assessments, /:id, /:id/sections/:sid/questions
│       ├── proctor.js         ← POST /proctor/verify
│       ├── sessions.js        ← GET/POST/DELETE /sessions/:sectionId
│       └── submit.js          ← POST /submit/:sectionId, GET /submit/:sectionId/result
├── frontend-api/              ← Drop these into your React src/
│   ├── api.js                 ← Single API client (auth, assessments, sessions, submit)
│   ├── App.jsx
│   ├── LoginPage.jsx
│   ├── ProctorVerifyPage.jsx
│   ├── AssessmentsPage.jsx
│   ├── TestSectionsPage.jsx
│   ├── MCQPage.jsx
│   └── QuestionListPage.jsx
├── .env.example
├── .gitignore
├── package.json
└── railway.toml
```

---

## Local setup

```bash
# 1. Install dependencies
npm install

# 2. Copy and configure environment
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env — set JWT_SECRET to a strong random string

# 3. Seed the database (creates faceprep.db with all data)
npm run seed

# 4. Start development server (auto-restarts on file changes)
npm run dev
# → http://localhost:4000
```

### Default credentials after seeding

| Role    | Email                    | Password    |
|---------|--------------------------|-------------|
| Admin   | admin@faceprep.com       | admin123    |
| Student | student@faceprep.com     | student123  |

Proctor code for the active assessment: **123456**

---

## Integrating the frontend files

1. Copy `frontend-api/api.js` → `your-react-app/src/api/api.js`
2. Replace these pages in `src/pages/` with the versions from `frontend-api/`:
   - `App.jsx` (goes in `src/`, not `src/pages/`)
   - `LoginPage.jsx`
   - `ProctorVerifyPage.jsx`
   - `AssessmentsPage.jsx`
   - `TestSectionsPage.jsx`
   - `MCQPage.jsx`
   - `QuestionListPage.jsx`

3. Add to your React `.env`:
```
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
```

---

## API Reference

All routes except `/api/auth/login`, `/api/auth/register`, and `/api/health` require:
```
Authorization: Bearer <token>
```

### Auth

| Method | Endpoint | Body | Returns |
|--------|----------|------|---------|
| POST | `/api/auth/login` | `{ email, password }` | `{ token, user }` |
| POST | `/api/auth/register` | `{ name, email, password }` | `{ token, user }` |
| GET  | `/api/auth/me` | — | `{ user }` |
| POST | `/api/auth/logout` | — | `{ ok }` |

### Assessments

| Method | Endpoint | Returns |
|--------|----------|---------|
| GET | `/api/assessments` | `{ active: [...], completed: [...] }` |
| GET | `/api/assessments/:id` | Assessment + sections (with `completed` flag per user) |
| GET | `/api/assessments/:id/sections/:sectionId/questions` | `{ section, questions }` |

### Proctor

| Method | Endpoint | Body | Returns |
|--------|----------|------|---------|
| POST | `/api/proctor/verify` | `{ code, assessmentId }` | `{ ok, assessmentId }` |

### Sessions (in-progress exam state)

| Method | Endpoint | Body | Returns |
|--------|----------|------|---------|
| GET    | `/api/sessions/:sectionId` | — | `{ answers, statuses, time_left }` or 404 |
| POST   | `/api/sessions/:sectionId` | `{ answers, statuses, time_left }` | `{ ok }` |
| DELETE | `/api/sessions/:sectionId` | — | `{ ok }` |

### Submit

| Method | Endpoint | Body | Returns |
|--------|----------|------|---------|
| POST | `/api/submit/:sectionId` | `{ answers, time_taken }` | `{ submission_id, score, total_marks, graded }` |
| GET  | `/api/submit/:sectionId/result` | — | `{ score, total_marks, time_taken, graded }` |

### Health

```
GET /api/health → { status: "ok", ts: 1234567890 }
```

---

## Deploy to Railway (free)

1. Push `faceprep-backend/` to a **new GitHub repo**

2. Go to [railway.app](https://railway.app) → New Project → Deploy from GitHub

3. Railway detects Node.js automatically and runs `npm start`

4. In Railway dashboard → your service → **Variables**, set:

```
PORT=4000
JWT_SECRET=your_long_random_secret_here
FRONTEND_URL=https://your-frontend.vercel.app
DATA_DIR=/tmp
```

> **Note on `DATA_DIR=/tmp`:** Railway's filesystem resets on each deploy.
> For a permanent database, add a Railway **Volume** (free tier available)
> and set `DATA_DIR` to the volume mount path (e.g. `/data`).
> Then run `npm run seed` once via the Railway console.

5. Copy the Railway public URL (e.g. `https://faceprep-backend.up.railway.app`)

6. In your React app's deploy (Vercel/Netlify), set:
```
VITE_API_URL=https://faceprep-backend.up.railway.app
```

7. After first deploy, run the seed from the Railway console:
```bash
npm run seed
```

---

## Database schema

```
users           id, name, email, password_hash, role, created_at
assessments     id, title, type, total_sections, total_questions, duration_mins, status, start_date
sections        id, assessment_id, title, total_questions, total_marks, duration_mins, type, position
questions       id, section_id, text, type, options (JSON), correct_idx, position
proctor_codes   id, code, assessment_id, expires_at
exam_sessions   id (user__section), user_id, section_id, answers (JSON), statuses (JSON), time_left
submissions     id, user_id, assessment_id, section_id, answers (JSON), score, total_marks, time_taken
```